# Ring sources check out LF, as they did in Ring++ (whose .gitattributes carried this rule for every .ring file, these included).
# Without it core.autocrlf rewrites them CRLF on checkout, `git status` calls them modified for ever while `git diff` shows nothing,
# and a court reading its own source by byte offset reads different bytes.
*.ring text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party sources check out BYTE-EXACT, never line-ending converted: their SHA256SUMS are claims about those bytes
# (Ring++ found core.autocrlf rewriting the grammar's 21 MB parser.c on checkout, so the copy no longer matched its release).
vm/vendor/** -text
